[
    {
        "content": "<p>See theorem 17 from these <a href=\"https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/teaching/2324/DenotSem/notes.pdf\">lecture notes</a>. For a continuous function <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f : D \\to D</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">D</span></span></span></span> where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">D</span></span></span></span> is an <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\omega</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.03588em;\">ω</span></span></span></span>-CPO, the least fixpoint <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{fix(f)}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">fix</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathrm\" style=\"margin-right:0.07778em;\">f</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> has property <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">P</span></span></span></span> if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">P</span></span></span></span> is admissible and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span></span></span></span> preserves <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">P</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.13889em;\">P</span></span></span></span>. I've looked around <code>ScottContinuous.lean</code>, <code>OmegaCompletePartialOrder.lean</code>, <code>Part.lean</code>, <code>Fix.lean</code>, and <code>LawfulFix.lean</code> but not sure if I'm missing it</p>\n<p>(edit: typo)</p>",
        "id": 587668026,
        "sender_full_name": "Tanner Duve",
        "timestamp": 1776657223
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>Thinking aloud on what's needed here:</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=OmegaCompletePartialOrder.fixedPoints.%CF%89Sup_iterate_le_fixedPoint#doc\">docs#OmegaCompletePartialOrder.fixedPoints.ωSup_iterate_le_fixedPoint</a> carefully avoids constructing the least fixed point in their statements (probably because it might not be computable)<ul>\n<li><code>(x : α) (h : x ≤ f x)</code> plays the role of \\bot in condition Thm.17(i), letting the theorem generalise to e.g. ℤ \\ ℕ.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Condition Thm.17(iii) chain-closed is more or the conditions of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=OmegaCompletePartialOrder.subtype#doc\">docs#OmegaCompletePartialOrder.subtype</a> , i.e. <code>subtype p h_p_is_chain_closed</code></li>\n<li>so the missing premise is Thm.17(ii).</li>\n</ul>\n</div></div>\n<p>So we probably want an analogue of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=OmegaCompletePartialOrder.fixedPoints.%CF%89Sup_iterate_mem_fixedPoint#doc\">docs#OmegaCompletePartialOrder.fixedPoints.ωSup_iterate_mem_fixedPoint</a> like so:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span> be a predicate on a ωCPO <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">α</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span>. (Write <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">≔</mi></mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>p</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">α_p \\coloneqq \\{a \\in α \\mid p\\, α\\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7167em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0037em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop\" style=\"position:relative;top:-0.0347em;\">:</span></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.0667em;\"></span></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span>.)<br>\nLet <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f : α → α</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span> be chain-continuous, and let <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x ≤ f(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7719em;vertical-align:-0.136em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.<br>\nIf <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span> is chain-closed, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p \\, x</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span>, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span></span></span></span> lifts (\"restricts\") to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_p : α_p → α_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9805em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">:</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7167em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0037em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7167em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0037em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, then<br>\n<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⋁</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bigvee_{n} f^n(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0497em;vertical-align:-0.2997em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"position:relative;top:0em;\">⋁</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.0017em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2997em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is a fixpoint of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9805em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.10764em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 588752794,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776818616
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've opened this PR here which makes an attempt at it. Seems like your suggestion is the right generalization. Will edit.<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38316\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38316</a></p>",
        "id": 588753709,
        "sender_full_name": "Tanner Duve",
        "timestamp": 1776819170
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh nice!</p>",
        "id": 588754203,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776819415
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Adding the rest of my thought dump for posterity:</p>",
        "id": 588754228,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776819431
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1060393\">Chris C</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Scott.20Induction/near/588752794\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>[...]</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>or, slightly rewriting:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Given <code>(p : α → Prop) (f : α →𝒄 α) (x : α)</code>, suppose that<br>\n* chain-closed: <code>OmegaCompletePartialOrder.subtype p hp</code> typechecks for some <code>hp</code><br>\n* <code>x</code> behaves like ⊥: <code>hfx : x ≤ f x</code>, <code>hpx : p x</code><br>\n* stable: <code>Subtype.map f hf: (subtype p hp) →  (subtype p hp)</code> typechecks (modulo coercions)<br>\nThen: <code>ωSup (iterateChain (↑(map f hf)) x h) ∈ Function.fixedPoints ⇑(map f hf)</code>, (modulo <em>many</em> coercions)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 588754279,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776819470
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Could any of this could be used to re-implement <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.nfp#doc\">docs#Ordinal.nfp</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 589395420,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776830820
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've always felt like that file duplicates more general order theory, but I'm not familiar enough with said theory to really do that generalization myself.</p>",
        "id": 589395879,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776831201
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(aside: Is the <code>a</code> in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.nfp#doc\">docs#Ordinal.nfp</a> docstring supposed to be <code>f</code>?)</p>",
        "id": 589396107,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776831361
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe the <code>a</code> refers to the unnamed <code>Ordinal</code> parameter</p>",
        "id": 589396197,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1776831458
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"459227\">Violeta Hernández</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Scott.20Induction/near/589395420\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could any of this could be used to re-implement <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ordinal.nfp#doc\">docs#Ordinal.nfp</a> ?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>quite possibly!<br>\nreferencing <a href=\"https://achimjungbham.github.io/pub/papers/handy1.pdf\">AJ94</a>, Thm 2.1.19 is <em>almost</em> perfect, except their \"pointed dcpo\" is a mathlib \"CompletePartialOrder\" (and IIUC <code>Ordinal.{u}</code> does not have a top element)</p>",
        "id": 589396340,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776831589
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>but what I described should generalise to a ConditionallyCompletePartialOrder, (search term: \"local dcpo\")</p>",
        "id": 589396436,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776831648
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In a general well-order of uncountable cofinality, for every normal function <code>f : α → α</code> and every <code>x : α</code> there is a least fixed point greater or equal to <code>x</code>, given by the supremum of the iterates <code>f^[n] x</code></p>",
        "id": 589396838,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776831934
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think you can generalize from well-order to conditionally complete linear order if you assume <code>x ≤ f x</code></p>",
        "id": 589396902,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776831985
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>per AJ94 Thm2.1.19, you can generalise to conditionally complete order, no linearity required</p>",
        "id": 589397024,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776832068
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(E.g. <code>α → ℕ∞</code> )</p>",
        "id": 589397148,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776832155
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"459227\">Violeta Hernández</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Scott.20Induction/near/589396838\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In a general well-order of uncountable cofinality, for every normal function <code>f : α → α</code> and every <code>x : α</code> there is a least fixed point greater or equal to <code>x</code>, given by the supremum of the iterates <code>f^[n] x</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The implication being that Ordinal.{u} has uncountable cofinality?</p>",
        "id": 589397389,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776832240
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(The interactions of Lean's type theory with ordinals/cardinals goes a little over my head)</p>",
        "id": 589397636,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776832328
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1060393\">Chris C</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Scott.20Induction/near/589397389\">ha dicho</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"459227\">Violeta Hernández</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Scott.20Induction/near/589396838\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In a general well-order of uncountable cofinality, for every normal function <code>f : α → α</code> and every <code>x : α</code> there is a least fixed point greater or equal to <code>x</code>, given by the supremum of the iterates <code>f^[n] x</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The implication being that Ordinal.{u} has uncountable cofinality?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37675\">#37675</a></p>",
        "id": 589398071,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776832647
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The approach <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Scott.20Induction/near/588754279\">above</a> for the directed case would certainly get \"<code>⨆ f^[n] x ≤ [any fixpoints ≥ x]</code>, so given well-foundedness, the only part missing from that approach is <em>existence</em> of fixpoints</p>",
        "id": 589398402,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776832868
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>which is exactly what uncountable cofinality gives, if I'm reading the definition right</p>",
        "id": 589398451,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776832888
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>or what normal function gives</p>",
        "id": 589398519,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776832917
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If <code>α</code> is a well-order of uncountable cofinality, then the set of fixed points of a normal (continuous + strictly monotone) function <code>f</code> is a club (closed and cofinal) set. Further, if the order type of <code>α</code> is the initial ordinal for a regular cardinal, every cofinal subset of <code>α</code> has the same order type of <code>α</code>, meaning you can \"enumerate\" the fixed points of <code>f</code> by a new function <code>g : α → α</code>. This is essentially what the ordinal derivative is.</p>\n<p>Does any of this generalize to DCPOs? Or do the theories of their fixed points just happen to be superficially similar?</p>",
        "id": 590110319,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776837884
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Superficial i think. The existence of fixed points for DCPOs is caused by the function space itself being <em>constructively</em> a DCPO, at which point we essentially \"take the sup\"</p>",
        "id": 590111987,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1776838079
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alright, that's good to know. Sorry for derailing this thread.</p>",
        "id": 590112858,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1776838384
    }
]